<title>USA: St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Monday, barrows and gilts were steady.</p>
<p>Interior Iowa only moved 88,000 Monday, producers back in the fields for Spring planting but packers bidding lower for hogs. Cut-outs turned a darker red yesterday, bellies 3.00-5.00 lower. Killers will just have to cut their chain speed some more, year to date slaughter already 6.4 percent below a year ago.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs	56.50-57.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs	55.00-56.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady. Top $51.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-500 lbs	48.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs	49.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs	50.00-51.00</p>
<p>    Boars:    300-700 lbs	40.00</p>
<p>		  200-300 lbs	41.00</p>
</text>
